    scenario:{chapter:3,sourceText:'I held the file out of his reach.',instruction:'Have Eden invite Felix to copy the incriminating page himself, turning a test of loyalty into a specific act of accountability.',rewriteText:'I held the file between us.\n\n“Copy it.”\n\nFelix looked at his grandmother’s signature.\n\n“Every line,” I said. “Your family does not get to become a footnote in someone else’s confession.”\n\nHe sat down. For the next twenty minutes, the only sound in the archive was a privileged man doing his own transcription.',continueText:'He made two copies and signed both. One went into my bag; the other he posted to a solicitor before he could decide the gesture was enough.\n\n“You may still dislike me,” he said.\n\n“I was planning to.”\n\nHe held the door while I carried the evidence through.',whatIfText:'Felix makes and distributes the record before the induction. The dean can no longer contain the evidence by expelling Eden. Trust improves through a verifiable act, while both students still lose access to stolen ability.',futureText:'Felix’s testimony arrived without a family crest. Eden corrected one date and returned it.\n\nAt Ada’s request, they met in a café rather than on campus. There were no portraits, no glass case, and nobody spoke of sainthood.\n\nAda chose the table by the open window. The others waited for her to sit.',bridge:'Felix copies the agreements; external counsel receives them early; the induction can expose rather than merely interrupt the extraction; Ada retains control of her public account.',titles:{rewrite:'Make him copy the signature',continue_block:'Evidence outside the gates',what_if:'What if Felix implicates his own family?',future_jump:'A table without portraits',roleplay_session:'Whose reputation are you protecting?'},delta:{before:'A rival offering private protection',after:'An ally accepting public responsibility',description:'Felix cannot substitute secrecy for care; his family’s role remains in the record.'},roleplay:{opening:'When you say you can protect me, do you mean me—or the version of this that leaves your surname intact?',reply:'I meant both. That was convenient of me. Tell me what needs copying, and do not let me call it courage.',narration:'Felix removes the signet from his writing hand and lays it beside the unsigned statement.',responses:['The archive key is mine. If they ask how you got in, I will answer before you have to.','My mother’s work may not all be hers. I need to know which parts, even if I dislike what knowing does to us.','Ada has agreed to see us on Tuesday. Agreed, not been scheduled. I am trying to learn the distinction before I make another useful mistake.']},alternative:{title:'What if Eden signs the renewal?',instruction:'Show the appeal of security and the immediate evidence of harm; do not turn complicity into a free power-up.',text:'The signature was beautiful. Eden had never written her own name so elegantly. Below the chapel, Ada’s finger stopped moving. Above it, the dean announced a permanent fellowship, and Ruth Ward began to clap because she thought her daughter was finally safe.'}},
